{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/837840-arcadian-commoners-and-others","id":837840,"title":"Arcadian Commoners and Others","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-26T18:16:35-08:00","id":837840,"title":"Arcadian Commoners and Others","content":"So, a question has come into my head. Many of the books agree that the Sidhe were not the only ones to flee to Arcadia; that with them went many Commoners. Indeed, it is possible that more Commoners went to Arcadia than Sidhe, given how many Sidhe took their retinues with them. We know, too, that some mortals and Kinain went, as Thomas the Rhymer famously returned. But aside from him, I can find no OTHER account of non-Sidhe returning from Arcadia.<br /> <br /> So what is the consensus on this, and will this be addressed in C20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:59:40-08:00","id":838625,"title":"","content":"As I've understood it, all the fae from Arcadia are sidhe. When the fae retreated to Arcadia, the kiths hadn't solidified as concrete splats. Instead you had the Firstborn, Inanimae and Changelings. But after the Shattering, the fae outside Arcadia became the Commoners and the fae inside became the Arcadian sidhe. Hence why only the sidhe seem to have returned from Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T08:51:57-08:00","id":838662,"title":"","content":"It might have to do with the arrogance of the sidhe. As the Shattering crushed trod after trod, the sidhe forced the other kiths to stand aside for their &quot;betters&quot;. Only after they evacuated were the Commoners allowed to try to escape, too. They were the sidhe, after all - they &quot;deserved&quot; first dibs.<br /> <br /> Given the general attitude of the Resurgence sidhe, it wouldn't surprise me to learn that the Arcadians did the same thing, when trying to evacuate <i>back</i> to Earth. Screwing the Commoners, just to save their own necks<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/837840-arcadian-commoners-and-others?p=838625#post838625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've understood it, all the fae from Arcadia are sidhe. When the fae retreated to Arcadia, the kiths hadn't solidified as concrete splats. Instead you had the Firstborn, Inanimae and Changelings. But after the Shattering, the fae outside Arcadia became the Commoners and the fae inside became the Arcadian sidhe. Hence why only the sidhe seem to have returned from Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't pick up second edition, but in first, the splats were already well-established before the Shattering. Each splat represents a different dream, from a different land, after all. Nobility, or travelers from afar, anonymous helpers or loved ones lost to the sea . . . And there are numerous canon examples - the merfolk and selkies were in charge of Silver's Gate, for example, and many are still upset with the sidhe for stealing it. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, in the good old days, inanimae and changelings were very rare. True fae could still walk openly among mortals, if they wished. It was only the Shattering that made such &quot;odd&quot; hobbies into a vital survival strategy, drastically boosting the numbers of fae fusing with humans (or objects).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T02:28:08-08:00","id":839031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/837840-arcadian-commoners-and-others?p=838662#post838662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't pick up second edition, but in first, the splats were already well-established before the Shattering. Each splat represents a different dream, from a different land, after all. Nobility, or travelers from afar, anonymous helpers or loved ones lost to the sea . . . And there are numerous canon examples - the merfolk and selkies were in charge of Silver's Gate, for example, and many are still upset with the sidhe for stealing it. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, in the good old days, inanimae and changelings were very rare. True fae could still walk openly among mortals, if they wished. It was only the Shattering that made such &amp;quot;odd&amp;quot; hobbies into a vital survival strategy, drastically boosting the numbers of fae fusing with humans (or objects).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is from DA:F. The kiths actually emerged after the Shattering, but because of some revisionism on the part of the Mists and the Dreaming, they actually stretched backwards and forwards through history from the moment they formed. That's the logic implied by DA to explain why kiths didn't exist in that setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T10:52:02-08:00","id":843517,"title":"","content":"A number of books state explicitly that Commoners DID go, though. The Gwydion information, for example, notes this. And the return of Thomas the Rhymer shows that even some Kinain went along, though admittedly he is probably a rare example. But the Gwydion information talks about their knights fighting to allow their retinues to escape to Arcadia. And this is not the only example of this sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:49:38-08:00","id":843708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/837840-arcadian-commoners-and-others?p=843517#post843517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A number of books state explicitly that Commoners DID go, though. The Gwydion information, for example, notes this. And the return of Thomas the Rhymer shows that even some Kinain went along, though admittedly he is probably a rare example. But the Gwydion information talks about their knights fighting to allow their retinues to escape to Arcadia. And this is not the only example of this sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another inconsistency, I guess. But there don't appear to be any Arcadian Commoners in the setting. Or, at least, there's no crunch for them. Perhaps you could just give them Banality's Curse in addition to any other kith flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}